      "http_status": 200,
      "api_response": {
        "answer": "If the automatic reload feature fails to work on Windows 10 when modifying `main.py`, you can consider the following steps based on reported issues:\n\n1. Ensure you are following the correct tutorial steps as outlined in the FastAPI README.md.\n2. Check if the issue is related to the `.iocp` (I/O Completion Ports) by reviewing any error messages that may appear when the server attempts to reload.\n3. If you encounter an `OSError` with a message like `[WinError 87] The parameter is incorrect`, this indicates a failure in the socket connection during the reload process. You may need to investigate socket configurations or permissions.\n4. Verify that your FastAPI and Python versions are compatible and up to date.\n5. Consider using a different method to run your FastAPI application, such as using a debugger configuration that includes the `--reload` parameter, and ensure that it is set up correctly.\n\nFor more specific troubleshooting, you may want to refer to related issues on GitHub, such as issues #618, #759, and #5244, which discuss similar problems with automatic reload on Windows 10.",
